  "term": "mental energy",
  "definition": "Mental energy, in competitive sport, refers to a person’s sense that they have enough cognitive, emotional, and motivational resources to meet performance demands. It is described as a multidimensional psychological resource linked with staying engaged, self-regulated, emotionally steady, and resistant to fatigue under pressure.",
